values ('bbbb0001-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'en', null, 'Graph Theory', 'Graphs are the language for anything made of things and the connections between them - friendships, roads, dependencies, and flows. This course builds from vertices and edges up through connectivity, trees, coloring, matching, traversals, planarity, shortest paths, and network flow, closing with a real problem modeled as a graph. Structure adapted from MIT OpenCourseWare 6.042 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0); all explanations original.', null, 'foundations', 20, true, 'math', '{bbbb0001-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c}')
on conflict (id) do nothing;

